model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway.accountPresentation {
    metadata {
      constraint "A catalog entry may name the tools each of its app's account requirements runs, by requirement. It describes the app only: it never declares credentials, changes providers or alters saved accounts. Where it names every requirement of a service section, each row says which of the other requirements' tools its account can't run, in place of naming the part it serves where the others run different tools, and in one sentence with any declared tool sections it can't run. Each method in the section's connect menu says which tools it reaches, and a label repeated by a requirement of the same name stays offered when the requirements run different tools. Where it names only some, rows make no such claim. Hosted and local read the field from the catalog entry they already load. The current hosted and local catalog-guidance result forwards requirementTools beside guidance and toolSections, so the shared renderer needs no extra discovery request or provider rewrite."
    }
  }
}
